<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29927" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑβραῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <u>Hebrew</u>: and as
			Subst., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a
			Hebrew</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
				11.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.5.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				2.71
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑ. ἐξ Ἑβραίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Phil.</u>
					3.5
				</span></i>
			, etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλληνιστής</span>, a
			Jew who used the Hebrew (<span class="entity">Aramaic</span>) language,
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				6.1
			</span></i>:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑβραϊκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
				<u>Hebrew</u>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
					23.38
				</span></i>
			 (s.v.l.):—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑβραΐς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, διάλεκτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					21.40
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					2.9.5
				</span></i>
			:—Verb <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑβραΐζω</span></b> , <i>speak Hebrew</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>BJ</u>
				6.2.1
			</span></i>:—Adv.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑβραϊστί</span></b> , <i>in the
				Hebrew tongue</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i>
			<i>Si.prol.,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Jo.
				19.20
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
